---
<LessonLayout title="Sacramentals and Popular Piety" cic={lessonRef} scripture={lessonScripture}>

<section class="content">

<h2>Big Question</h2>

<p class="big-question">Do the 'little things' of faith matter?</p>


<p>
Blessed Carlo Acutis, a boy born in 1991, had an unusual hobby. While other teenagers played video games, he researched Eucharistic miracles. He catalogued over a hundred of them from around the world, created a website to share them, and organized everything with meticulous care. His secret? "The Eucharist is my highway to heaven," he said. When asked about his life plan, he answered simply: "To always be united with Jesus." The Church has always blessed things: water, ashes, palms, medals, scapulars, rosaries. These sacramentals are not magic. They are extensions of the sacramental life, small signs that immerse our daily existence in the grace of Christ. The material world is not an enemy to escape but a vehicle of grace.
</p>


</section>

<section class="content">

<h2>Understanding the Mystery</h2>

<p>The Church teaches us through the Catechism.</p>

<div class="depth-box depth-box--semilla">
<h4 class="depth-box__title">Activity</h4>
<p>Reflect on how this teaching applies to your daily life.</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h2>Biblical Foundation</h2>

<p>Sacred Scripture reveals God's plan for us.</p>

<div class="depth-box depth-box--brotes">
<h4 class="depth-box__title">Connection</h4>
<p>Read the related passages and meditate on their meaning.</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h2>For Reflection</h2>

<ol>
<li>What does this teaching mean for your life right now?</li>
<li>How has your understanding changed after this lesson?</li>
<li>What concrete step can you take this week?</li>
<li>What gift of God have you discovered in this topic?</li>
